The schema contains an event, participating organisations, an event effect, a named event location, its coordinate point, and a hierarchy of administrative locations. The event is an Action identified by event_id_cnty, which is populated and unique in the samples. The four actor columns represent Organisation subjects because their values name military forces, commands, and armed groups; actor names are used as their identifiers, while empty associated-actor values cause those subjects to be skipped.

Fatalities are modeled as a separate ActionEffect because Action has the object property has result and the schema supplies the effect quantity. The event location is a Location identified by its latitude and longitude, preventing same-named places from merging. Its coordinates populate a separate AbsolutePoint connected through has geometry. Admin2, admin1, country, and region are separate Location subjects connected by part of. Admin3 is not used because it is empty in all samples and using it in the location path would silently drop the hierarchy links.

The event classification columns map to classification code: disorder_type, event_type, sub_event_type, and interaction all explicitly denote event classifications at different granularities. civilian_targeting is also treated as a classification flag, though with lower confidence because the ontology has no specifically civilian-targeting property. The source column is not mapped to source identifier: “source” names the reporting organization, whereas source identifier is qualified by “identifier”; event_id_cnty is the actual identifier. Similarly, timestamp is not mapped to observation date time because it is not described as an observation and appears distinct from event_date.

No AlternateIdentifier entity is created for event_id_cnty or iso. The ontology’s AlternateIdentifier class requires a standard-and-value structure; event_id_cnty is already the event’s direct source identifier, while iso has only one implicit standard rather than a separate scheme column.

Every IRI transformation below was checked against its referenced subject transformation: actor_, effect_, location_, point_, admin2_, admin1_, country_, and region_ expressions are character-for-character identical. All classes and properties used occur verbatim in the ontology, and no unused transformation key is emitted.

